│ │                                         │    - She bought a pair of shoes for     │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │ $50.                                    │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │    - She also bought a dress for $200.  │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │    - So, total money Sara spent = $50 + │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │ $200 = **$250**                         │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │                                         │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │ 2. **Rachel's Budget:**                 │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │    - Rachel wants to spend twice as     │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │ much as Sara.                           │                     │           │ │
│ │                                         │    - So, double of $250 = 2 × $250 =    │                     │           │ │
